<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Dairy Queen Fountain Beverage Lineup (2026)</h2>
    <p>Dairy Queen operates as a dedicated Coca-Cola fountain partner, serving ice-cold fountain classics designed to cut through the richness of Stackburgers, hot fries, and soft-serve treats. While exact spigot lineups vary slightly between classic "Treat" kiosks and full-scale "Grill &amp; Chill" restaurants, visitors can depend on core national staples:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Coca-Cola® Classic:</strong> The iconic, crisp cola pairing for savory burgers and salty fries.</li>
      <li><strong>Diet Coke® &amp; Coca-Cola Zero Sugar®:</strong> Crisp, effervescent cola taste with 0 calories and 0g sugar across all cup sizes.</li>
      <li><strong>Sprite® &amp; Sprite Zero®:</strong> Caffeine-free, refreshing lemon-lime fizz that provides a clean palate cleanser between dessert courses.</li>
      <li><strong>Dr Pepper® &amp; Diet Dr Pepper®:</strong> The beloved blend of 23 signature flavors, offering rich spicy-sweet notes.</li>
      <li><strong>Barq's® Root Beer:</strong> Bold and bubbly with real bite—often customized by guests with a dollop of vanilla soft serve for an impromptu float.</li>
      <li><strong>Minute Maid® Lemonade &amp; Fanta® Orange:</strong> Tart and fruity options popular with kids and non-cola drinkers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sizes, Calorie Ranges &amp; Pricing Breakdown</h2>
    <p>Dairy Queen fountain soft drinks start at an accessible $2.11 for a Small cup and scale smoothly through generous thirst-quenching sizes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Small (16 oz · $2.11 · 0–190 cal):</strong> Great for lighter lunches or when paired alongside a mini Blizzard.</li>
      <li><strong>Medium (21 oz · $2.49 · 0–250 cal):</strong> The standard size included with most adult combo meals.</li>
      <li><strong>Large (32 oz · $2.89 · 0–310 cal):</strong> Ideal for long road trips and serious hydration.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Beverage Face-Off: Soft Drinks vs. Other DQ Drinks</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Drink Category</th><th>Starting Price</th><th>Calorie Span</th><th>Key Advantage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Fountain Soft Drinks</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$2.11</td><td>0–310 cal</td><td>Fast, crisp, 0-calorie options available, dine-in refills</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Arctic Rush / Misty Slush</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$2.39</td><td>~220–380 cal</td><td>Bold icy fruit flavors (Blue Raspberry, Cherry, Strawberry)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Milk / Chocolate Milk</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$1.49</td><td>100–160 cal</td><td>Kid-friendly sealed cartons packed with calcium and protein</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hand-Spun Shakes</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>530–920 cal</td><td>Indulgent dessert beverage spun with real milk and DQ soft serve</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Value Strategy: Why You Should Never Buy Soda A La Carte</h2>
    <p>If you plan on enjoying food at Dairy Queen, ordering a fountain drink separately at $2.11–$2.89 is rarely the most cost-effective move. Both DQ's signature combos and value promotions bundle a beverage at significant savings:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The $7 Meal Deal:</strong> Includes an entrée (Original Cheeseburger or 3-piece Chicken Strips), hot fries, a 21 oz drink, and a small sundae for just $7.00. Buying these items a la carte would easily exceed $11.00.</li>
      <li><strong>Combo Upgrades:</strong> Upgrading any Stackburger or Chicken Strip basket to a full combo adds a drink and fry for roughly half the individual retail cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Dine-In Free Refills:</strong> Most traditional Grill &amp; Chill dining rooms feature customer-accessible fountain machines offering complimentary refills during your stay. (Drive-thru orders do not include free refills).</li>
    </ul>

